# Current theses

## Thesis T-migrated-tools: Preserve reviewed project guidance
Status: accepted
Based-on: user-reviewed-contract-migration

### Guidance
<folder_context path="tools">

<settled_decision name="Release-channel manifests come from immutable assets" id="channel_checksums">
`release-channels.py` renders the Homebrew formula and Scoop manifest from the `checksums.txt`
already attached to the named GitHub Release. A recovery rebuild is never a checksum source.
Missing expected archive names or malformed SHA-256 values are fatal; never guess or overwrite a
release asset.
</settled_decision>

<settled_decision name="Homebrew uses a formula until macOS artifacts are notarized" id="homebrew_quarantine">
The tap publishes `Formula/git-a2a.rb`. The formula installs the checksum-verified release binary
and conditionally removes `com.apple.quarantine` from that exact installed file before testing it.
The absence of the attribute must remain a successful, idempotent case.
</settled_decision>

<system_invariant name="Channel output is deterministic and self-testing">
Given the same tag and `checksums.txt`, the renderer writes identical bytes. Formula and Scoop URLs
name tag-specific archives and every hash is looked up by that exact name. Prerelease package URLs
retain the full tag while the binary reports the canonical embedded version. Formula and Scoop
tests execute `git-a2a --version`; Scoop preserves separate amd64 and arm64 hashes.
</system_invariant>

<settled_decision name="Package-manager repositories are shared collections">
`neprel/homebrew-tap` and `neprel/scoop-bucket` are shared repositories. Release automation owns
only `Formula/git-a2a.rb` and `git-a2a.json`; preserve every unrelated file and package.
</settled_decision>

<settled_decision name="Skill distribution is a checked copy" id="skill_distribution">
`sync-skill.py` treats `skills/git-a2a/SKILL.md` and its three canonical document references as
inputs. It makes a byte-identical static-site skill tree and `/.well-known/skills/index.json`.
There is no CLI setup copy, harness-specific projection, or release-version coupling. Check mode
fails on copy drift, and generated JSON uses deterministic UTF-8 bytes with LF endings.
</settled_decision>

<verification_and_unit_test_criteria name="Release and documentation channels">
- Fixture checksums drive both release-channel manifests and every architecture hash.
- A missing expected archive fails instead of emitting a partial manifest.
- Recovery skips GoReleaser's Homebrew/Scoop publishers and derives channels from immutable assets.
- Homebrew and Scoop execute the installed binary with `--version`.
- `make docs-check` validates schema 2 conformance and the single canonical skill copy; it does not
  generate contact, trust, MCP, setup, transcript, or schema 1 artifacts.
</verification_and_unit_test_criteria>

<reusable_automation_script name="Pinned native lifecycle matrix">
`tools/native-lifecycle/run.py` is the single tracked entry point for native adapter execution.
It snapshots the current tracked and non-ignored untracked working tree, including unstaged bytes,
builds Linux binaries in the pinned builder image, and mounts both snapshot and binaries read-only
into pinned per-toolchain containers. Containers receive no host credentials, SSH agent, or Docker
socket; fixtures and Git remotes are local to their temporary container environment. Results are
written by the invoking host user beneath the selected output directory as one log per executed row
plus machine-readable and Markdown summaries. A selected row is a failure when its mandatory tool
is missing, its test is skipped, or the test command exits nonzero.
</reusable_automation_script>

<verification_and_unit_test_criteria name="Native lifecycle evidence">
- The matrix enumerates every registered family and concrete detection variant, including npm,
  Python, Hackage, Gradle, and MSBuild variants plus the Git submodule adapter.
- A row records the pinned image, observed tool version, OS/architecture, exact command, status,
  and log path. Cross-build and command-mock results are never labeled native PASS.
- Consolidation applies reports in input order and selects the latest executed row. FAIL and
  BLOCKED replace earlier results, NOT RUN does not, and histories from consolidated inputs are
  flattened and retained without treating the selected row as a new attempt.
- The Python CI gate invokes the same public-CLI lifecycle entry point as a local runner and does
  not silently skip a missing manager.
</verification_and_unit_test_criteria>

</folder_context>

### Rationale
Migrated from the pre-2.0 HINT source format without changing its guidance.

